The discrete Fourier transform (DFT) may be calculated if the Fourier transform
of a time series is desired at a single frequency or over a limited frequency range
as shown below
dt  0.001;
tmax  2.0;
t  0:dt:tmax;
A  2*sin(2*pi*150.0*t)  5*sin(2*pi*333.0*t);
nmax  length(t);
fmin  300;
fmax  350;
mmax  1000;
Ftx  zeros(1,mmax);
f  linspace(fmin,fmax,mmax);
for m  1:mmax
for n  1:nmax
Ftx(m)  Ftx(m)  A(n)*exp(-1i*2*pi*f(m)*n*dt);
end
end
